	quests: [
		{
			dependencies: ["210200000000000E"]
			description: [
				"&9&lAge IV · Power & Automation.&r"
				""
				"Heat generators got you started. They will not carry you to the stars. This Age builds the real power spine - Powah reactors and a wind farm - and a Hostile Neural Network that farms mobs without a single spawner."
				""
				"Everything past here drinks Forge Energy. Time to make a lot of it."
			]
			icon: "powah:energizing_orb"
			id: "2103000000000001"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2103000000000101"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 50
			}]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.5d
			subtitle: "&7Build the power spine"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2103000000000201"
				title: "Electrify the sky"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "&9Age IV · Power & Automation"
			x: -12.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2103000000000001"]
			description: [
				"The keystone bridge turns Sky Dust into &eUraninite&r - Powah's reactor fuel, and an ore that will never spawn in the void. Bank a few; the reactor eats them."
				""
				"&e&lThis is a bridge recipe, not a real supply.&r SkyForge exists to break chicken-and-egg problems: Powah needs uraninite, uraninite needs an overworld, and you do not have one. The keystone gets you started - it does not scale."
				""
				"&e&lThe scalable answer is Mystical Agriculture.&r Uraninite seeds turn reactor fuel into a crop you harvest. If you intend to run reactors seriously - and Age IV assumes you will - get that farm going early rather than bridging one ingot at a time."
				""
				"&e&lWhat it feeds:&r Powah's &7Uraninite &8→&7 Uranium&r line, and from there the Reactor tiers that carry your grid from Age III to the fission plant in Ascension."
				""
				"&7Powah reactors consume fuel continuously while running, unlike the Thermo and Wind generators you have been leaning on. Budget for a steady supply before you commit your base to one.&r"
				""
				"&8The same keystone bridges osmium for Mekanism and certus for AE2. One block, three tech trees unlocked."
			]
			icon: "powah:uraninite"
			id: "2103000000000002"
			rewards: [{
				count: 8
				id: "2103000000000102"
				item: "powah:uraninite"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Reactor fuel from nothing"
			tasks: [{
				count: 4L
				id: "2103000000000202"
				item: "powah:uraninite"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Bridged Uranium"
			x: -10.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2103000000000002"]
			description: [
				"The &eEnergizing Orb&r crafts Powah's tiered materials - toss items into the field, feed it power, get the next tier out."
				""
				"Every Powah machine climbs the same ladder: &7Basic &8→ &7Hardened &8→ &7Blazing &8→ &7Niotic &8→ &7Spirited &8→ &7Nitro&r. This is where you build up it."
			]
			icon: "powah:energizing_orb"
			id: "2103000000000003"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2103000000000103"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 50
			}]
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "&7Craft the tiered materials"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2103000000000203"
				item: "powah:energizing_orb"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9The Energizing Orb"
			x: -8.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2103000000000003"]
			description: [
				"A &eThermo Generator&r sat over lava makes passive FE forever, no fuel runs required. Drop a few and stop thinking about power for a while."
				""
				"&e&lIt runs on a temperature difference, not on burning fuel.&r Lava on one side, cooler air or water on the other, and it produces indefinitely. The lava is &lnot consumed&r - one bucket powers it forever."
				""
				"&e&lWhich makes it perfect here.&r You already have a lava source for your cobble generator, and SkyForge gives you lava synthesis. Free heat you were making anyway."
				""
				"&7Surround it with water or place it in a cold biome to widen the temperature gap - output goes up. A generator sitting in the Nether next to lava produces almost nothing, because everything around it is already hot.&r"
				""
				"&e&lIt is slow but utterly reliable&r - no fuel logistics, no moving parts, no maintenance. Build a bank of them as your baseline grid and let the reactors handle peaks."
				""
				"&8Between this and wind, you can run all of Age III without ever crafting a fuel-burning generator."
			]
			icon: "powah:thermo_generator_basic"
			id: "2103000000000004"
			rewards: [{
				count: 4
				id: "2103000000000104"
				item: "minecraft:blaze_rod"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Passive power over lava"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2103000000000204"
				item: "powah:thermo_generator_basic"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Free Heat"
			x: -6.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2103000000000003"]
			description: [
				"&eWind Generators&r love the void - they scale with altitude, and you live at the top of the sky. Place a field of them high up for cheap, clean Mekanism power."
				""
				"&e&lThis is the one generator a skyblock is actually good at.&r Output scales with Y level, and you start higher than most players ever build. Free real estate."
				""
				"&e&lThe rules that matter:&r"
				"&7- &fOutput rises with altitude.&7 Build them on your highest platform, not at base level."
				"&7- &fThey need open sky.&7 Blocks directly above kill them."
				"&7- &fThey do not need fuel, water, or attention.&7 Ever."
				"&7- &fSome dimensions have no wind at all&7 - do not plan a Moon base around them."
				""
				"&e&lThey are individually weak.&r One will not run a Purification Chamber. The answer is quantity - a field of twenty is trivially cheap, silent, and needs nothing from you again."
				""
				"&7Wire them into an Energy Cube rather than straight to machines. Wind output is steady but small, and the buffer is what turns a trickle into something that can handle a burst of demand.&r"
				""
				"&8Cheap enough to be your first real grid, weak enough that you will still want Powah reactors later. Build both."
			]
			icon: "mekanismgenerators:wind_generator"
			id: "2103000000000005"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2103000000000105"
				type: "xp_levels"
				xp_levels: 3
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Power that scales with height"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2103000000000205"
				item: "mekanismgenerators:wind_generator"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Sky Power"
			x: -6.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2103000000000005"]
			description: [
				"An &eEnergy Cube&r buffers your generators so machines never starve between gusts. Your first real battery - bigger storage comes with the Induction Matrix."
				""
				"&e&lWhy a buffer is not optional.&r Generators produce a steady trickle; machines demand in bursts. Wire a Purification Chamber straight to a wind farm and it stutters. Put a cube between them and the same farm runs it smoothly, because the cube absorbs the peaks."
				""
				"&e&lConfigure the sides.&r Right-click, open the config tab, and set each face to input or output. A cube with every side on the same mode will happily push power back into your generators and do nothing useful. This is the most common wiring mistake in Mekanism."
				""
				"&e&lFour tiers&r - Basic, Advanced, Elite, Ultimate - each holding far more and transferring faster. Upgrade in place with the tier installers; you keep the stored charge."
				""
				"&7They are portable. A charged cube in your inventory will refill Free Runners, a Meka-Tool or a jetpack in the field.&r"
				""
				"&8Put one next to any machine that runs intermittently. It is cheaper than a bigger generator and fixes the same problem."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:basic_energy_cube"
			id: "2103000000000006"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2103000000000106"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Buffer your grid"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2103000000000206"
				item: "mekanism:basic_energy_cube"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Store Some Power"
			x: -4.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
